# sapintegrationsuite_partner_authorized_user (Resource)

An authorized user maps an inbound communication user (the user or client that sends messages
to your tenant) to the partner ID (Pid) it may act as. A user maps to exactly one Pid; a Pid can
have several users. This resource manages only the mapping; the user itself, its OAuth client
or certificate belong to BTP and are not managed here.

**Status:** supported. Backed by `AuthorizedUsers` of the Partner Directory API.

## Prerequisites

- An OAuth client with the role `AuthGroup_TenantPartnerDirectoryConfigurator`.
- A partner ID (Pid) chosen by you. It does not have to exist: SAP creates a Pid the first time
  an entry references it, and there is no resource for partners themselves.

## Lifecycle

| Operation | What happens |
|---|---|
| Create | Creates the mapping for `user`. |
| Read | Reads the Pid the user is authorized for. |
| Update | A changed `partner_id` repoints the mapping in place. |
| Replacement | Changing `user` or `runtime_location_id` creates a new mapping. |
| Delete | Deletes this mapping only. |

